index 0000000..3d2fb7b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp32/components/muse/wake/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Wake word model
+
+`wake_word.tflite` is microWakeWord's "Hey Jarvis" v2 model by Kevin Ahrendt, from
+[esphome/micro-wake-word-models](https://github.com/esphome/micro-wake-word-models)
+(`models/v2/hey_jarvis.tflite`, Apache License 2.0). Its settings (`hey_jarvis.json`):
+probability cutoff 0.97, sliding window 5, 10 ms feature step, ~22.9 KB tensor arena.
+
+To use another model ("Okay Nabu", "Alexa", "Hey Mycroft", or one you train), replace the
+file (keep the name) and set `CONFIG_MUSE_WAKE_WORD_NAME`, `CONFIG_MUSE_WAKE_CUTOFF`
+(cutoff x 255) and `CONFIG_MUSE_WAKE_WINDOW` from its JSON.
